## 9. Dark Mode Implementation

### Activation

Apply dark mode via `data-theme="dark"` on the `<html>` or root element.

```javascript
// Toggle dark mode
document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', 'dark');
```

### Key Overrides

```css
[data-theme="dark"] {
    /* Backgrounds shift to deep purple tones */
    --bg-primary: #0f0a1f;
    --bg-secondary: #15102b;
    --bg-tertiary: #1f1740;
    
    /* Bright purple gets lighter for visibility */
    --bright-purple: #c44dff;
    
    /* Text inverts to white */
    --text-primary: #ffffff;
    --text-secondary: #cccccc;
    
    /* Borders darken */
    --border-primary: #2a2a2a;
    --border-secondary: #404040;
}
```

### Chart Dark Mode

```javascript
// Update Plotly charts for dark mode
function applyDarkModeToChart(plotId) {
    Plotly.relayout(plotId, {
        'font.color': '#ffffff',
        'xaxis.tickfont.color': '#ffffff',
        'xaxis.linecolor': '#404040',
        'yaxis.tickfont.color': '#ffffff',
        'yaxis.gridcolor': 'rgba(60, 60, 60, 0.5)',
        'paper_bgcolor': 'transparent',
        'plot_bgcolor': 'transparent'
    });
}
```

### Logo Switching

```css
[data-theme="dark"] #wordmark-logo,
[data-theme="dark"] img[src*="wordmark.png"] {
    content: url('/static/darkwordmark.png');
}
```

