## 11. Accessibility

### Focus States

All interactive elements must have visible focus indicators:

```css
:focus {
    outline: 2px solid var(--bright-purple);
    outline-offset: 2px;
}

/* For buttons with custom focus */
button:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--bright-purple);
    outline-offset: 2px;
}
```

### Color Contrast

- Body text on light background: #222222 on #ffffff (15.9:1) ✓
- Body text on dark background: #ffffff on #0f0a1f (15.2:1) ✓
- Purple accent on white: #ad35fa on #ffffff (4.6:1) — Use for large text/icons only
- Error coral on white: #FF6B5A on #ffffff (4.0:1) — Pair with icon or bold text

### Screen Reader Considerations

- Always include descriptive `alt` text for data visualizations
- Use `aria-label` for icon-only buttons
- Provide text alternatives for color-coded information
- Use semantic HTML elements (`<main>`, `<nav>`, `<article>`)

