## 14. Writing Style

### Tone Guidelines

- **Be direct**: "12% increase in theft reports" not "There appears to be a notable uptick"
- **Be neutral**: Present data, not opinions
- **Be precise**: Use exact numbers when available
- **Be accessible**: Avoid jargon; explain technical terms when necessary
- **Be humble**: Acknowledge data limitations and uncertainty

### Formatting Conventions

- **Numbers**: Use commas for thousands (1,234,567)
- **Percentages**: One decimal place for precision (12.3%)
- **Dates**: "January 2024" or "Jan 2024" (month-year format)
- **Times**: 12-hour format with am/pm
- **Currency**: $1,234,567 (with commas)

### Microcopy Examples

| State | Message |
|-------|---------|
| Loading | "Loading chart data..." |
| Error | "Unable to load data. Please try again." |
| No data | "No data available for this period." |
| Success | "Data updated successfully." |
| Confirmation | "Are you sure you want to delete this?" |

