## 16. Implementation Checklist

When building new components or templates, verify:

- [ ] Uses CSS custom properties for colors (not hardcoded values)
- [ ] Includes dark mode support via `[data-theme="dark"]` overrides
- [ ] Uses correct font stack (Inter for headings, IBM Plex Sans for body)
- [ ] Follows spacing system (multiples of 4px)
- [ ] Has visible focus states for accessibility
- [ ] Includes loading, error, and empty states
- [ ] Uses semantic HTML elements
- [ ] Is responsive across breakpoints
- [ ] Charts follow Plotly styling conventions
- [ ] Links/accents use brand purple (`#ad35fa`)
- [ ] Errors/warnings use warm coral (`#FF6B5A`)
- [ ] Success/positive indicators use spruce green (`#4A7463`)

